# Cloud for ISO / nested VM work

On the Apple silicon Mac: do not use local Docker `linux/amd64` or
`qemu-system-x86_64` (TCG) as the gate for building the live ISO or wiping a
throwaway disk. Use the `gcloud` or `aws` CLI on an x86_64 Linux VM (KVM).

On Cursor Cloud Agent VMs (`uname -m` is `x86_64` and `/dev/kvm` exists):
local `./scripts/build-iso.sh` and KVM QEMU are native. Nested Docker needs
`fuse-overlayfs` in `/etc/docker/daemon.json`. Prefer `sudo docker` unless
this user is already in the `docker` group.

Local pytest and `python3 -m beamo_wipe --demo` are always fine.
